Code of Absolute Conflict
-------------------------

The development of this userland is a brutal process. Your code will be torn
to shreds, your logic will be mocked, and your architectural decisions will
be compared to building a suspension bridge out of wet noodles.

Know that this happens because:
1. We want code that actually works, not code that makes you feel validated.
2. If you fake a syscall the kernel does not have, you are dead to us.
3. If you vendor upstream source into ports/, you are also dead to us.
4. "It compiled on my machine" is an immediate grounds for public execution.

If you feel personally abused, offended, or your delicate ego has suffered
catastrophic failure due to technical feedback, that is entirely your problem.
Please forward your complaints, tears, and emotional trauma reports to:

    nobody@nowhere.com
    (or directly to /dev/null via plaintext email)

All tickets will be processed in the order they are ignored.

As a contributor, try to keep in mind the immortal words:
"Write working C code, don't fake syscalls, and get the fuck out of my tree."
